  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "theorem biased_gamblers_ruin (k N : ℕ) (p : ℝ) (hp : 0 < p ∧ p < 1 ∧ p ≠ 1/2) (hk : 0 < k ∧ k < N) : ruinProbability k N p = ((p/(1-p))^(N-k) - 1) / ((p/(1-p))^N - 1)",
    "plain": "For a biased random walk with step probability p ≠ 1/2, the probability of ruin (reaching 0 before N) starting from k is (1-(q/p)^k)/(1-(q/p)^N) where q = 1-p. This generalizes the fair-games-theorem-oq-02 result for p = 1/2.",
